abstract: >-
  Fullseye is a numpy-native library of typed classical image-processing and
  geometric-vision operators (2-D and 3-D; 2,088 operators in the machine-readable index:
  931 single-input 2-D operators, 17 n-ary and 1,140 in the typed ledgers), with an evolutionary pipeline-design mode
  evaluated under honest held-out gates, a Physical-AI perception stack
  (stereo -> depth -> point cloud -> 6-DoF pose), and an HDevelop-style IDE
  (Fullseye Studio). Every operator carries a machine-readable Markdown note
  (contract, references, license, version fingerprint) designed to double as a
  retrieval corpus for AI assistants and as a reproducible, citable methods reference.
keywords:
  - image processing
  - machine vision
  - explainable algorithms
  - robotics perception
  - evolutionary computation
